{"id":"src/lib/employees/admin/api.ts","pkg":"src/lib/employees","kind":"module","lines":112,"commentLines":15,"header":["THE EMPLOYEE MANAGER'S REQUESTS (step 66a). I use one handler for every operation the panel can ask; the route (src/app/api/employees/admin/route.ts) only brings the logged-in person and the database. The person comes from the LOGIN SESSION and from nowhere else: I ignore whatever the browser says about itself (a ticket, a name, a role). The rules are enforced here AND again inside the database transaction (store.ts), so the panel hiding a button is a courtesy, never the protection. logged out -> 401 logged in, no authority -> 403 for everything except \"me\" an authorised executive -> look up, add and change employees and read the history; NOT delete, NOT authorise or withdraw, and NEVER the two dates (birth, joining) the HOD of C&IT (SUPERADMIN_TICKETS) -> everything, the dates included"],"symbols":[{"name":"ApiContext","kind":"interface","exported":true,"line":20,"generics":"","extends":"","doc":[],"members":[{"kind":"field","name":"actor","line":21,"type":"Actor | null","optional":false,"readonly":false,"doc":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"db","line":22,"type":"EmpDb","optional":false,"readonly":false,"doc":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"findByName","line":23,"type":"(name: string) => Promise<EmployeeResult[]>","optional":false,"readonly":false,"doc":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"findByTicket","line":24,"type":"(ticket: string) => Promise<EmployeeResult[]>","optional":false,"readonly":false,"doc":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"photos","line":26,"type":"import(\"@/lib/employees/photo/storage\").PhotoStorage","optional":true,"readonly":false,"doc":["This is where the photos are kept (the photo goes with the employee when he is deleted); absent in the tests that do not need it."]}],"id":"aa24d3868b-ApiContext","usedBy":[]},{"name":"ApiReply","kind":"interface","exported":true,"line":28,"generics":"","extends":"","doc":[],"members":[{"kind":"field","name":"